{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>They were ashamed, for they trusted</b> — their heart; the meaning concerns those who trusted." "<b>They came to it</b> — to the place, for עד can be in the feminine, like ולא עוד תשורנו מקומו." "<b>And the meaning of the streams</b> — that the caravans are ashamed when they arrive at a place where they expected water to be there, and they are thirsty; likewise, my brothers have betrayed me."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:59.071257950Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}